---
// FAQSection.astro - Common Questions section
---

<!-- FAQ Section -->
<section class="py-24 px-4 sm:px-6 bg-gradient-to-br from-gray-50 to-white">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <div class="text-center mb-12" data-aos="fade-up">
      <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">
        Common Questions
      </h2>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600">
        Operational and clinical questions — answered directly
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-4" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
      <!-- FAQ 1 -->
      <details
        class="group bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow duration-300"
      >
        <summary
          class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer p-6 hover:bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl transition-colors"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 pr-4">
            How quickly can we start receiving patients?
          </h3>
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 ml-2">
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6 text-gray-400 group-open:text-[#cc9933] group-open:rotate-180 transition-all duration-300"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-6 pb-6">
          <div class="pt-4 border-t border-gray-100">
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              You could be receiving patients in as little as 2-3 weeks. Here's
              why it's so fast: Our digital onboarding system lets you review
              and sign everything online in about 15 minutes—no paperwork, no
              lawyers, no delays. The self-service portal walks you through each
              step. The 2-3 week timeline? That's just for standard
              credentialing that every network requires. But unlike the old days
              of paper contracts and phone tag, your part is done in minutes,
              not weeks. Sign today, start credentialing tomorrow, receive
              patients in weeks.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-4 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-green-600">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20">
                <path
                  fill-rule="evenodd"
                  d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z"
                  clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
              </svg>
              <span>Average time to first patient: 2-3 weeks</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <!-- FAQ 2 -->
      <details
        class="group bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow duration-300"
      >
        <summary
          class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer p-6 hover:bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl transition-colors"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 pr-4">
            What volume increase should we expect?
          </h3>
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 ml-2">
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6 text-gray-400 group-open:text-[#cc9933] group-open:rotate-180 transition-all duration-300"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-6 pb-6">
          <div class="pt-4 border-t border-gray-100">
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              Our AnciCare partners typically saw 20-40% volume increases. With
              USRad, we're targeting similar results using the same proven
              patient acquisition methods that delivered 168,000+ patient
              visits. Results vary by market, available appointment slots, and
              local competition.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-4 bg-blue-50 rounded-lg p-4">
              <p class="text-sm text-blue-800">
                <strong>Pro tip:</strong> Centers that dedicate specific time blocks
                to USRad patients typically see the highest volume increases.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <!-- FAQ 3 -->
      <details
        class="group bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow duration-300"
      >
        <summary
          class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer p-6 hover:bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl transition-colors"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 pr-4">
            Are there any costs to join USRad?
          </h3>
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 ml-2">
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6 text-gray-400 group-open:text-[#cc9933] group-open:rotate-180 transition-all duration-300"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-6 pb-6">
          <div class="pt-4 border-t border-gray-100">
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              No. Just like AnciCare, joining USRad is completely free for
              qualified centers. No setup fees, no monthly charges, no hidden
              costs. We only succeed when you succeed—our revenue comes from
              successfully connecting patients with your center.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 gap-4">
              <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-lg p-3 text-center">
                <svg
                  class="w-8 h-8 text-green-600 mx-auto mb-1"
                  fill="currentColor"
                  viewBox="0 0 20 20"
                >
                  <path
                    fill-rule="evenodd"
                    d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z"
                    clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
                </svg>
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-green-800">$0 Setup</p>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-lg p-3 text-center">
                <svg
                  class="w-8 h-8 text-green-600 mx-auto mb-1"
                  fill="currentColor"
                  viewBox="0 0 20 20"
                >
                  <path
                    fill-rule="evenodd"
                    d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z"
                    clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
                </svg>
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-green-800">$0 Monthly</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>

    <!-- FAQ 4 — anchor target from ReferralWorkflow -->
    <details
      id="physician-order"
      class="group bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow duration-300"
    >
      <summary
        class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer p-6 hover:bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl transition-colors"
      >
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 pr-4">
          Does a valid physician order come through before a patient is
          scheduled?
        </h3>
        <div class="flex-shrink-0 ml-2">
          <svg
            class="w-6 h-6 text-gray-400 group-open:text-[#cc9933] group-open:rotate-180 transition-all duration-300"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          >
            <path
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              stroke-width="2"
              d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
          </svg>
        </div>
      </summary>
      <div class="px-6 pb-6">
        <div class="pt-4 border-t border-gray-100">
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            Yes — always. USRad requires a valid physician order before any
            patient is scheduled at your facility. During our verification step,
            we confirm the ordering physician, the prescribed exam type, and
            patient eligibility. No order, no appointment. This is
            non-negotiable in our process and mirrors the clinical intake
            standards your center already operates under.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-4 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-[#003087]">
            <svg
              class="w-5 h-5 flex-shrink-0"
              fill="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 20 20"
            >
              <path
                fill-rule="evenodd"
                d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z"
                clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
            </svg>
            <span>Physician order verified before every scheduling event</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </details>

    <!-- FAQ 5 -->
    <details
      id="hipaa-compliance"
      class="group bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow duration-300"
    >
      <summary
        class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer p-6 hover:bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl transition-colors"
      >
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 pr-4">
          Who handles the HIPAA Business Associate Agreement?
        </h3>
        <div class="flex-shrink-0 ml-2">
          <svg
            class="w-6 h-6 text-gray-400 group-open:text-[#cc9933] group-open:rotate-180 transition-all duration-300"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          >
            <path
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              stroke-width="2"
              d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
          </svg>
        </div>
      </summary>
      <div class="px-6 pb-6">
        <div class="pt-4 border-t border-gray-100">
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            USRad operates as a HIPAA Business Associate and a BAA is executed
            as part of the credentialing process — before your center receives
            any patient. The agreement is included in your digital onboarding
            packet and covers all patient data handled by USRad on your behalf.
            Your center never handles USRad member financial data, and USRad
            never accesses your clinical records or systems.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-4 bg-blue-50 rounded-lg p-4">
            <p class="text-sm text-blue-800">
              <strong>Compliance note:</strong> The BAA is executed at credentialing,
              not after your first patient. Your compliance team can review it before
              you sign.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </details>

    <!-- FAQ 6 -->
    <details
      class="group bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow duration-300"
    >
      <summary
        class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer p-6 hover:bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl transition-colors"
      >
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 pr-4">
          Does joining USRad affect our existing payer contracts?
        </h3>
        <div class="flex-shrink-0 ml-2">
          <svg
            class="w-6 h-6 text-gray-400 group-open:text-[#cc9933] group-open:rotate-180 transition-all duration-300"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          >
            <path
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              stroke-width="2"
              d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
          </svg>
        </div>
      </summary>
      <div class="px-6 pb-6">
        <div class="pt-4 border-t border-gray-100">
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            No. USRad operates in the cash-pay segment — patients arrive with a
            physician order and have already arranged their own payment through
            the USRad platform. These patients are not billed through your
            existing payer relationships. There is no overlap with your
            insurance contracts, no balance billing, and no claims filing on
            your end. Your payer agreements remain completely independent.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-4 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-green-600">
            <svg
              class="w-5 h-5 flex-shrink-0"
              fill="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 20 20"
            >
              <path
                fill-rule="evenodd"
                d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z"
                clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
            </svg>
            <span>Zero impact on existing payer contracts or credentialing</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </details>

    <!-- FAQ 7 -->
    <details
      id="no-show-policy"
      class="group bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow duration-300"
    >
      <summary
        class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer p-6 hover:bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl transition-colors"
      >
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 pr-4">
          What happens if a USRad patient no-shows?
        </h3>
        <div class="flex-shrink-0 ml-2">
          <svg
            class="w-6 h-6 text-gray-400 group-open:text-[#cc9933] group-open:rotate-180 transition-all duration-300"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          >
            <path
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              stroke-width="2"
              d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
          </svg>
        </div>
      </summary>
      <div class="px-6 pb-6">
        <div class="pt-4 border-t border-gray-100">
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            USRad patients pre-arrange their own payment before their
            appointment is confirmed at your facility. This structure produces a
            96% show rate across our network — significantly above the industry
            average for self-pay patients. In the rare case of a no-show, your
            center is not exposed to a collections situation. The appointment
            slot simply becomes available again.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-4 bg-green-50 rounded-lg p-4">
            <p class="text-sm text-green-800">
              <strong>96% show rate</strong> — because patients have pre-arranged
              payment before the appointment is confirmed at your facility.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </details>

    <!-- FAQ 8 -->
    <details
      id="contract-terms"
      class="group bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow duration-300"
    >
      <summary
        class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer p-6 hover:bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl transition-colors"
      >
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 pr-4">
          What are the contract terms and length of commitment?
        </h3>
        <div class="flex-shrink-0 ml-2">
          <svg
            class="w-6 h-6 text-gray-400 group-open:text-[#cc9933] group-open:rotate-180 transition-all duration-300"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          >
            <path
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              stroke-width="2"
              d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
          </svg>
        </div>
      </summary>
      <div class="px-6 pb-6">
        <div class="pt-4 border-t border-gray-100">
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            Contract terms are provided during the digital onboarding process
            and available to review before signing. There is no long-term volume
            commitment required. Centers may adjust their availability and
            participation at any time through the provider portal.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-4 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-green-600">
            <svg
              class="w-5 h-5 flex-shrink-0"
              fill="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 20 20"
            >
              <path
                fill-rule="evenodd"
                d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z"
                clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
            </svg>
            <span
              >No long-term volume commitment — adjust participation anytime</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </details>

    <!-- FAQ 9 -->
    <details
      id="modalities"
      class="group bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow duration-300"
    >
      <summary
        class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer p-6 hover:bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl transition-colors"
      >
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 pr-4">
          Which imaging modalities does USRad support?
        </h3>
        <div class="flex-shrink-0 ml-2">
          <svg
            class="w-6 h-6 text-gray-400 group-open:text-[#cc9933] group-open:rotate-180 transition-all duration-300"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          >
            <path
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              stroke-width="2"
              d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
          </svg>
        </div>
      </summary>
      <div class="px-6 pb-6">
        <div class="pt-4 border-t border-gray-100">
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            USRad currently supports MRI, CT, X-ray, and ultrasound at
            participating ACR-accredited facilities. Additional modalities may
            be confirmed during onboarding based on your center's equipment and
            accreditation.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-4 bg-blue-50 rounded-lg p-4">
            <p class="text-sm text-blue-800">
              <strong>ACR accreditation required.</strong> Specific modality availability
              is confirmed during the credentialing process.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </details>

    <div class="text-center mt-12" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="200">
      href="/provider/faq" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[#003087]
      hover:text-[#cc9933] font-semibold transition-colors group" >
      <span>View all FAQs</span>
      <span class="group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">→</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
